{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-143460",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that \n\n$$\nP(X\\in A\\,|\\,Y=y)={\\int }_{A}{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ is the conditional probability density function of $X$ given $Y=y.$ \n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(\\frac{1}{4}<X<\\frac{1}{2}\\,|\\,Y=\\frac{5}{8}) & ={\\int }_{1/4}^{1/2}{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y=\\frac{5}{8})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/4}^{1/2}\\frac{2x}{{(\\frac{5}{8})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{64}{25}{\\int }_{1/4}^{1/2}2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{64}{25}[{x}^{2}]_{1/4}^{1/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{64}{25}(\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{1}{16}) \\\\  & =\\frac{64}{25}(\\frac{3}{16}) \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
